Z||000003||LEE498||05-14-99||07:42 AM||||Mid 14's all motor with automatic should'nt be that hard,just a little exspenive.It's going to take a little more than 200hp to do it tho.you're going to need a stall converter,2500-2800 rpm,for a killer take off,a shift kit is mandatory! To get close to 200hp you'll have to port and polish the head's and intake and install a higher lift cam.That will get you closeer,about 170-185hp.A 3.1 swap will get you there in no time.(190-220hp<br>) depending on cam and head work and your wallet!!
Z||000004||Pretender||05-14-99||03:20 PM||||where do i go about buying a stall converter?.i've never seen one for these cars..
Z||000005||ezsurf||05-14-99||06:11 PM||||Pretender,<br>Stall converter is just another name for torque converter.  If your car is an automatic, it has a torque converter.  A higher rpm torque (stall speed) converter simply allows your engine to turn at a higher rpm (where it is producing more HP) before it engages the transmission.  This will, of course, lower your ET at the strip.
Z||000006||LEE498||05-14-99||06:50 PM||||PRECISION INDUSTRIES is the company that makes them,hell they'll make any stall you want from 2000-4500 whatever you need.Just for a mesily $514.35! I have an 3000 stall in mine, with a shift kit and let me tell you it's a day and night differance.Takeoff is GREATLY improved i mean tire smoking take off's!! Here's there number(901-466-0267) that's they'er tech department they'll answer any ?'s you may have.   
